While the reduction in polymorphing could be gotten by a polymorph-immune
wand of nothing, a wand of everything has a couple of other interesting
features.

When you engrave with it, it picks a random effect, so it's hard to
identify this way -- makes all the wands a little riskier since until
you've used a wand a couple times, you can't be sure it isn't going to
turn out to be a wand of wonder.

And once you've identified it as a wand of everything, it's still something
of a mixed blessing.  When you're desperate (or overly cocky) you can try
it, but often it will not help.

	You zap the floating eye with a wand named every...
	The red dragon hits...
	You zap the red dragon with a wand named every...
	The invisible red dragon hits...
	You zap the invisible red dragon with a wand named every...
	The red dragon hits...
	The rope golem hits...
	The fire giant hits...
	The nymph stole a blessed +6 long sword named Excalibur!

Of course, with my bad luck, it'd be even worse than this scenario!  :-)

I think it should be called a wand of wonder, though; at least, this is what
it's called in rogue.  Seems like this name could lead to a better fortune
cookie.
